@startuml
title Say Swear - current shared Java application use cases
left to right direction
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
actor Player
actor "Microphone device" as Mic <<device>>
actor "sherpa-onnx\nstreaming ASR" as ASR <<external runtime>>
actor "Local SemIf /\nQwen3.5 4B" as Model <<external service>>

rectangle "Say Swear: one shared game / agent / control core" {
  usecase "UC01 - Play Using\nContinuous Voice Control\nF01-F10" as UC01
  usecase "UC02 - Play Using\nCLI Commands\nF01, F04-F10" as UC02
  usecase "UC03 - Interpret\nContextual Command\nF05, F09" as UC03
  usecase "UC04 - Correct an\nActive Command\nF06, F09" as UC04
  usecase "UC05 - Execute Combined\nor Timed Command\nF07, F08, F09" as UC05
  usecase "UC06 - Fall and\nReturn to Start\nF09, F10" as UC06
}

Player --> UC01
Player --> UC02
Mic --> UC01
ASR --> UC01
Model --> UC01
Model --> UC02
Model --> UC03
Model --> UC04
Model --> UC05

UC03 ..> UC01 : <<extend>>\ncontextual instruction
UC03 ..> UC02 : <<extend>>\ncontextual instruction
UC04 ..> UC01 : <<extend>>\nnew correction
UC04 ..> UC02 : <<extend>>\nnew correction
UC05 ..> UC01 : <<extend>>\ncombined / timed instruction
UC05 ..> UC02 : <<extend>>\ncombined / timed instruction
UC06 ..> UC01 : <<extend>>\nplayer leaves safe path
UC06 ..> UC02 : <<extend>>\nplayer leaves safe path

note bottom of UC03
  "other way" uses initial held directions;
  "keep going" preserves current controls;
  "again" repeats stored movement semantics,
  including a fresh timed action after expiry.
end note
note bottom of UC06
  Deterministic cancellation and recovery.
  Every fall returns to Level.start().
  No checkpoint or AI navigation.
end note
note top of UC01
  JavaFX is voice-first; its optional text field
  also submits natural-language instructions.
  One frontend is selected per launch.
end note
@enduml
